Current-main cross-system findings (17 October 2026)
Mainnet Supabase
Project: ribpntyqdleytsyktdfb. The audit was read-only.
Existing objects include public.withdrawal_requests, public.withdrawal_payout_attempts, public.stakes, public.albukhr_fee_policies, legacy claim/finish RPCs, the approved withdrawal queue, and albukhr_security review/manual-paid RPCs.
withdrawal_payout_attempts currently has one row per request by unique index and includes id, withdrawal_request_id, network, status, attempt_count, lease_until, payment_id, txid, last_error, and timestamps. It has no lease_token, payment_creation_started_at, or submission_started_at. The four RPC names invoked by the v2 service are absent: claim_a2u_withdrawal_payout_v2, record_a2u_withdrawal_payout_progress_v2, fail_a2u_withdrawal_payout_v2, finalize_a2u_withdrawal_payout_v2.
Both current create_my_withdrawal_request overloads are EXECUTE-granted to service_role; the five-argument overload is called by POST /api/withdrawal-request. The old definitions reserve/check against the original stake/reward amount and block pending/approved duplicates, but do not subtract previous paid withdrawals from remaining capital/reward. Any corrected migration must preserve signatures and service-role-only grants until callers/ACLs are reverified.
albukhr_security.mark_withdrawal_paid requires auth, AAL2, active Finance/Super Admin role, approved status and a TXID, then marks the row paid and writes an admin audit record. It does not currently check withdrawal_payout_attempts for an active or uncertain A2U attempt.
The legacy claim_a2u_withdrawal_payout/finish_a2u_withdrawal_payout are SECURITY DEFINER functions. They do not provide v2 attempt-id plus fencing-token protection. Do not use them as the new worker's completion contract.
Mainnet API (albukhr-api/main)
src/a2u-payout-service.js calls missing v2 RPCs and reads the durable markers returned by the claim RPC.
src/pi-a2u-client.js keeps a source-level Mainnet hard gate disabled. It dynamically imports pi-backend only after the gate and other checks.
src/financial-gateway.js still contains a second legacy A2U executeWithdrawalPayout implementation and /api/pay-withdrawal route. It uses a process-local activePayouts set and does not delegate to the single v2 service. This must be reconciled before any A2U activation.
server.js does not mount src/a2u-worker.js. scripts/a2u-payout-cron.js exists, but render.yaml has only a web service and no Cron service.
package.json does not declare pi-backend and npm run check currently skips the A2U service/client/worker/cron files. render.yaml shows npm install, not yarn install; prior v1.2 documentation incorrectly referred to Yarn deployment.
POST /api/withdrawal-request verifies the Pi identity server-side and invokes the five-argument request RPC. Preserve this route and all unrelated U2A/investment routes.
No GET /api/withdrawal-history was found in the current API source.
User side (albukhr-app/main)
investor-dashboard.html links to withdraw.html.
withdraw.html does not exist in the current main tree retrieved for this audit.
No withdrawal-creation/history caller was found in the current app tree's indexed paths/search.
This does not prove the deployed site is identical to main; confirm deployment source or page mapping before replacing any UI.
Admin side (albukhr-admin/main)
admin-withdrawals.html and js/admin-withdrawals.js run a manual flow: pending -> approve/reject -> Finance/Super Admin sends Pi manually -> enters TXID -> mark_withdrawal_paid. AAL2 and the server-side DB checks remain in place. The queue contains pending/approved rows and does not expose the A2U attempt status, so the UI currently cannot reliably tell the finance administrator whether an automation attempt exists.
Pi platform gate
Official Advanced Payments docs state A2U is currently Testnet-only. The Launch guide mentions an Outgoing Wallet application for eligible Mainnet apps. This requires fresh official confirmation and ALBUKHR-specific eligibility before any activation.
